cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this research proposal, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "ScaleGap-TH: Model Size versus Self-Supervised Pretraining in Thai Audio Deepfake Detection under G.711 Telephone Coding"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "punyo_o"
repository-code: "https://github.com/punyopan/ysc"
url: "https://github.com/punyopan/ysc"
license: MIT
version: 0.4.0
date-released: 2026-08-19
abstract: >-
  A focused research proposal separating two factors the audio-deepfake
  literature leaves entangled: whether robustness to G.711 telephone coding in
  Thai comes from model size or from self-supervised pretraining. Uses a
  size-by-pretraining detector panel including a student distilled on clean data
  only, a bandwidth-only control separating low-pass filtering from companding,
  paired difference-in-differences estimates, and an on-device deployment
  measurement.
keywords:
  - audio deepfake detection
  - Thai speech
  - accuracy-compute trade-off
  - knowledge distillation
  - self-supervised pretraining
  - efficient inference
  - on-device deployment
  - G.711
  - telephone speech
  - anti-spoofing
